WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.300
Mind Your Decisions. I'm Presh Talwalkar.

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:08.700
Solve for the value of each color
in the following arithmetic problem.

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:13.240
Each color represents a different digit from 0 to 9.

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:16.380
I thanks Lucas for suggesting this problem.

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:20.840
It originally appeared as a Belgian Olympiad problem

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:23.660
with the letters M, A, and T.

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:27.360
Pause the video if you'd like to give this problem a try

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:31.200
and when you're ready, keep watching
to learn how to solve this problem.

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:46.720
We'll get started by focusing on the letter M.

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:49.820
Suppose M equals 5.

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:54.380
In that case, the sum will be at least 1500.

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:57.760
And this is going to be too large of the value

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:00.420
because we need the sum to be 1416.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.960
Therefore M equals 5

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:06.420
produces a sum that's too large and it's not possible.

00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:10.680
The same logic is true for M
greater than or equal to 5.

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:13.120
We can eliminate all of these possibilities.

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:15.960
What if M equals 3?

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:21.300
In that case, the largest value of the sum will be 1197.

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:25.240
And that's too small because we need 
the sum to be 1416.

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:29.580
Therefore M equals 3 cannot be a possibility

00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:33.640
and M less than or equal to 3 can also be eliminated.

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:37.180
What remains is M is equal to 4.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:40.060
This will simplify our calculation.

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:42.780
If we substitute M is equal to 4

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:45.640
we know that just from the terms involving M

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:47.620
we get a sum of 1204.

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:50.040
We subtract those out

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:52.060
we get the resulting sum

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:53.720
of 212

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:55.560
and we have a new problem.

00:01:56.340 --> 00:01:58.460
We now need to solve for A and T.

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.620
Let's focus on T.

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:05.640
In the unit's column, T plus T can either equal 2

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:07.120
or it can equal 12.

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:09.420
Consider the first case.

00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:11.600
If T plus T equals 2

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:13.400
then T is equal to 1.

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:16.300
Which then means the entire problem

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:17.880
has to be 10 A

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:19.320
plus 10 A plus 1

00:02:19.460 --> 00:02:21.460
plus 11 is equal to 212.

00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:25.640
This means 20 A equals 200 and A is equal to 10.

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:30.140
But that's not possible because A has to be 
a single-digit from 0 to 9.

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:34.240
Therefore we must have T plus T is equal to 12.

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:36.500
This means T is equal to 6.

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:38.400
And we can then go ahead and solve

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:40.540
that A must be equal to 7.

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:43.520
Therefore this is the answer to the problem.

00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:45.320
M is equal to 4,

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:48.220
A is equal to 7, and T is equal to 6.

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:51.300
And we can, in fact, verify this does work out.

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:56.940
Thanks for making MindYourDecisions 
one of the best channels on YouTube.

00:02:56.980 --> 00:03:01.460
As always thanks for watching 
and thanks for your support.

